{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-synthesis", "file": "references/sparse-pattern-completion-lesson.md", "content": "# Selective sparse-pattern completion: unresolved row-selection rule

This session supplied eight heterogeneous demonstrations for a task whose test was a 29×24 grid with sparse 7-patterns on background 5. In several demonstrations, a few cells at the right ends of selected rows/regions changed from background to 1. Examples included right-edge row tails (2 or 4 cells, depending on grid width), a small 2×2 corner patch, and other selective edge blocks. Many visually similar rows and repeated-looking counterparts remained untouched. Full-width bands were often unchanged except for a single anomalous cell, which then became 1. The final pair reinforced that tail extension occurs only for selected patterns, not every non-background row.

Two test submissions were wrong: first the input was preserved, then alternating background cells in a row were recolored. Neither demonstrates a validated rule. The selection predicate remains unresolved. For future instances, classify this as sparse-pattern completion/repair, but do not fill all row tails, all repeated rows, or a broad rectangle. Transcribe all changed and unchanged cells from each pair, form competing explicit selection hypotheses, and reproduce every demo cellwise before testing. If the demo cap is reached without a rule, submit only the best-supported candidate and never label it validated.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u096/system/state/hermes/skills/arc/arc-demo-synthesis/references/sparse-pattern-completion-lesson.md"}

