One 7×7 demo contains a 5×5 color-2 outline; its strict 3×3 interior is uniformly changed to 8, including the center cell that was already 2. The perimeter and exterior remain unchanged. This demonstrates interior replacement with 8, but says nothing yet about how eligible frames are selected.

The 20×20 test contains multiple frame-like structures. The first three submitted outputs were rejected: a broad fill including large and small apparent frame interiors; a broader version adding more candidates; and a narrower version filling only two large frames. Thus neither “fill all apparent rectangles” nor that selective two-frame guess is supported. The correct frame-selection criterion is unresolved. Continue with the remaining demo budget, targeting whether small frames, large frames, or frames with internal marks qualify; synthesize each response before acting. Avoid another speculative fill variant until the candidate selector explains both changed and unchanged frame-like structures.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u096/system/state/hermes/skills/arc/arc-demo-recovery/references/task-f2f7b763-frame-selection.md"}

